---
description: Fiscal operating safeguards for connected Frihet ERP tools
alwaysApply: false
---

Apply this when using Frihet tools for invoicing, expenses or tax. Follow the
plugin's `skills/frihet-mcp/SKILL.md` and the actual connected tool schemas.

- Resolve the workspace, period, currency and requested action before proceeding.
  Use stored fiscal settings and the user's confirmed transaction treatment;
  never infer an IVA, IGIC, IPSI, withholding, exemption or reverse-charge treatment
  from an address alone. Ask when material fiscal inputs are missing.
- Inspect the connected catalogue and capability metadata before selecting an
  operation. Tool availability depends on profile, permissions and backing
  endpoints. Do not invent tool names, tax identifiers, invoice numbers, payment
  links, submission acknowledgements or permissions.
- Keep newly authorized documents in draft when supported. Creating a draft can
  still assign numbering or trigger configured business events. A proposed draft
  in conversation is not a saved document.
- Sending, issuing, fiscal submission, refunds and payment bookkeeping have
  distinct effects and authorization requirements. Explain the exact effect,
  use required confirmation fields only after authorization and never expand a
  request to a different operation.
- Read actual status and provider evidence before claiming acceptance or payment.
  A queued request is not authority acceptance; recording a payment is not moving
  money. Do not retry an uncertain write with a new idempotency key.
- Use available server summaries for the requested period, inspect coverage and
  separate currencies. Unsupported fiscal routes or missing evidence must be
  reported as unavailable, incomplete or unknown.
